prompt:
Inventory icons of three new fish for a mobile farm game, in exactly the same style as the reference fish icons (soft painted, thick dark-brown outline, smooth clean outlines, warm saturated colors, glossy highlight, big friendly round eye, side view facing left like the reference fish). Separate objects in one row, each centered in its own equal cell, filling most of its cell, no text, no plates or frames:
1) a bream: a broad, very deep and flat oval body, small head and small mouth, shiny silvery-bronze scales with a golden sheen, grey-brown fins, forked tail;
2) a pike: a long slender predatory fish, olive-green back with rows of pale yellow oval spots, cream belly, a long flat duck-bill snout with a few small white teeth, dorsal fin set far back near the tail, reddish-brown fins;
3) a catfish: a big heavy fish with a wide flat head and a wide mouth, two long whiskers and a few short ones, tiny eyes, smooth scaleless dark grey-brown skin with darker mottling, pale cream belly, a long low fin along the back half of the belly, rounded tail. The catfish looks the biggest and the bream the smallest.

Inventory icons of fishing bait for a mobile farm game, in the same style as the reference icons (soft painted, thick dark-brown outline, smooth clean outlines, warm saturated colors, glossy highlight). Do not use any green color on the objects (no leaves, no grass, no moss). Separate objects in two rows (three on top, two below), each centered in its own equal cell, front view, filling most of its cell, no text, no plates or frames unless described:
1) worms: a small open round tin can full of dark brown soil with three pink earthworms curling out over the rim;
2) dough bait: a round ball of soft pale-yellow dough with a fingerprint dent on top, a small pinched-off piece and a few bread crumbs beside it;
3) a golden jig: a tiny shiny golden fishing lure shaped like a teardrop with a small red bead and a sharp little hook, hanging on a short piece of fishing line, with two small sparkles;
4) live bait: a small dented metal bucket with blue water and two tiny silver minnow fish peeking out of the water;
5) night crawlers: a small open wooden box with dark soil and dry brown leaves, three big fat dark-pink-brown night crawler worms, much longer and thicker than ordinary worms, hanging over the edge.
